    "article": {
      "title": "Getting started with CSS grid",
      "paragraphs": [
        "Grid layout divides a page into rows and columns. Unlike flexbox, which arranges items in one direction at a time, grid places them across both, which makes it a good fit for whole-page layouts.",
        "Column widths often use the fr unit, which stands for one share of the space left in the container. For example, grid-template-columns: 1fr 2fr splits the remaining space into three parts and gives two of them to the second column.",
        "Items can also span several cells, so a magazine-style layout takes only a few lines of code."
      ],
